(area "lang" :when "the agent is about to write or fix lisptc code, or a form just failed or returned something unexpected")

(memory "internal/lang/syntax" :when "the agent is about to write lisptc that needs exact syntax: quoting, quasiquote, dotted pairs, strings, keywords, numbers or symbol names; or a form just failed to read, or read as something else than meant"
  "Syntax detail.
- Quote: 'x same as (quote x) — x unevaluated.
- Quasiquote: leading backtick same as (quasiquote x) . Inside, ,x unquotes, inserts evaluated x; ,@x unquote-splicing, splices a list.
  Example: (a ,(+ 1 2) ,@(list 3 4)) evaluates to the list a 3 3 4.
- Lists: (a b c) . Dotted pair: (a . b) is one cons cell.
- Strings: \"...\" with escapes \\\\ \\\" \\n \\r \\f \\b \\t \\v. No character type: \"character\" is one-character string; char-code and friends take them.
- Keywords: :foo self-evaluating, interned, so (eq :a :a) is t.
- Numbers: see internal/lang/numbers. nil and () same value: empty list and false. t is canonical true.
- Comments: there is no comment syntax — prose around forms is the comment. ; is ordinary symbol character, so \"; note\" inside a form is code.
- Symbols: any token not number, string, keyword, nil or t. / and - legal in names, e.g. string-split, acme/get_widget.")

(memory "internal/lang/prose-asides" :when "the agent is about to write a remark, an aside or parentheses next to its code, or its last reply ran nothing, or prose was just run as code and failed with undefined"
  "Asides and parens in prose.
Aside whose head names nothing — (see below) , (one, two,
  three) — reads as prose, comes back as skipped note. Mistake the reader
forgave, not a way to write. Forgiveness narrow, unpredictable: anything shaped
like a call runs. Keyword argument, string literal, nested call, or slashed or
underscored name with no words around it — (server/tool :key \"value\") , dummy
names — is code whatever is missing. (see below) skips; (see
  \"below\") raises undefined: see. Tool of unloaded server: undefined: error to
fix, not a skip. Reply of only asides ran nothing, ends the loop.
Stray paren in prose still reads as code, so never write one; paren smiley unsayable.")

(memory "internal/lang/data-types" :when "the agent is about to test for an empty or false value or branch on a value's type, or a type check just returned something unexpected, such as zero or an empty string read as true"
  "Data types.
- Cons cell — pair (car . cdr) ; list is chain of cells ending in nil.
- Symbol — interned name; gensym and make-symbol make uninterned ones, printed #:name.
- Keyword — :foo, self-evaluating.
- String — text.
- Hash table — mutable map, keys compare by equal. Prints #<hash-table n>.
- Vector — mutable indexed sequence. Prints #<vector 1 2 3>.
- Function / closure / macro — from lambda, defun, defmacro.
- Secret — tainted string wrapper, only when secrets extension loaded.

Test emptiness with null or not. Never rely on 0 or \"\" being false — they are TRUE.")

(memory "internal/lang/special-forms" :when "the agent is about to use a special form, a loop or deep recursion, or a step just failed with a stack overflow or a form that did not evaluate as expected"
  "Evaluated specially, not as function calls. Complete list:

| Form | Shape | Meaning |
|------|-------|---------|
| quote | (quote x) | Return x unevaluated, written 'x. |
| progn | (progn e...) | Evaluate in order, return the last. |
| cond | (cond (test body...) ...) | First clause with non-nil test: eval its body, return last, or the test value if no body. Else nil. |
| setq | (setq name val ...) | Assign val to variable name, one or more pairs. Returns last value. Defines or updates a global if name isn't a local. |
| lambda | (lambda (args...) body...) | Anonymous function, a closure over the current scope. |
| macro | (macro (args...) body...) | Anonymous macro. Top-level only; normally use defmacro. |
| quasiquote | (quasiquote x) | Template with unquote and unquote-splicing, see internal/lang/syntax. |
| try | (try
  body
  (catch (e)
    handler...)) | Eval body; on error, bind e to the error value and run the handler. |

Tail calls optimized: tail recursion and loop macros never overflow the stack.
Iterate with tail-recursive helpers or loop macros.")

(memory "internal/lang/numbers" :when "the agent is about to do arithmetic or division, or a result just came back as a float, a ratio or an integer where another was expected"
  "NUMBERS
- Integer literal is exact bigint: 42.
- Decimal or exponent makes inexact float: 42.0, 4.2e1.
- + - * keep exactness: bigint with bigint gives bigint. ANY float makes the
  result float, \"float contagion\": (+ 1 2) is 3,
(+ 1 2.0) is 3.0, (* 2 3) is 6, (* 2 3.0) is 6.0.
- / is ALWAYS float, even evenly divisible: (/ 6 2)
is 3.0. Exact integer division: truncate, gives bigint:
(truncate 6 2) is 3.
- Integer-valued float prints 3.0; bigint prints 3.
- = and eql compare numerically across types: (= 3 3.0) is t.
- Divide by zero: / follows JS, (/ 1 0) is Infinity, (/ 0 0) is NaN, no error.
  Integer truncate, % and mod on bigints throw. Guard divisors.")

(memory "internal/lang/arithmetic" :when "the agent is about to call a math function: add, subtract, multiply, divide, remainder, rounding, power, root, gcd, min, max, or a number test such as even or zero; or one just failed with a wrong argument"
  "Arithmetic built-ins:
- (+ n...) sum, 0 if none · (* n...) product, 1 if none ·
(- n m...) subtract, or negate one arg · (/ n m...) float divide.
- (% x y) remainder, sign of x, alias rem · (mod x y) modulo, sign of y ·
(truncate x [y]) toward zero, gives bigint.
- (< x y) primitive less-than. Prelude adds (> x y) , (>= x y) , (<= x y) ,
(/= x y) and (= x y) .
- Predicates: (numberp x) · (zerop n) · (plusp n) · (minusp n) ·
(evenp n) · (oddp n) , last two integers only.
- (abs n) · (min n m...) · (max n m...) · (1+ n) · (1- n) , keep exactness.
- (floor x [y]) · (ceiling x [y]) · (round x [y]) give bigint, like
  truncate. round takes tie to even: (round 2.5) is 2.
- (expt b p) exact for integer b and p >= 0, else float · (sqrt n) float ·
(gcd n...) · (lcm n...) .
- (parse-integer s) decimal string to bigint, error otherwise.")

(memory "internal/lang/lists" :when "the agent is about to build, read or change lists, pairs or symbols, or test a value with atom, eq, eql, stringp or numberp; or a list call just failed or returned nil unexpectedly"
  "Lists and pairs:
- (car x) first · (cdr x) rest · (cons a b) new cell · (list x...) .
- (length x) length of list or string, bigint.
- (rplaca cell x) and (rplacd cell x) destructively set car and cdr, aliases
  setcar and setcdr.

Predicates:
- (atom x) true if not cons · (eq x y) identity · (eql x y) identity or
  numeric and string equality, alias = · (stringp x) · (numberp x) .

Symbols:
- (gensym) fresh uninterned symbol · (make-symbol name) · (intern name) ·
(symbol-name sym) .")

(memory "internal/lang/hash-vectors" :when "the agent is about to keep keyed data in a hash table or index into a mutable vector, or a hash or vector call just failed"
  "Hash tables:
- (make-hash-table) · (gethash key table [default]) · (puthash key value table)
· (remhash key table) · (clrhash table) · (hash-has-key key table) ·
(hash-table-count table) · (hash-table-keys table) ·
(hash-table-values table) · (hash-table-alist table) · (hash-table-p x) .
  Keys by equal: \"a\", 2 and 2.0, (list 1 2) all work. Order is insertion.

Vectors:
- (vector x...) · (make-vector n [init]) · (aref v i) · (aset v i x) ·
(vector-push x v) appends, returns index · (vector-to-list v) ·
(list-to-vector list) · (vectorp x) . Index past end errors.
- (length x) , (elt seq i) and (subseq seq start [end]) take list, string or
  vector.")

(memory "internal/lang/strings" :when "the agent is about to read, build, compare, upcase, pad or convert text or turn a value into a string, or a string call just failed or returned the wrong text"
  "Strings:
- (char s i) one-char string at i, or nil · (concat s...) concatenate
  · (string-upcase s) · (string-downcase s) .
- (string< a b) · (string> a b) order by code point · (string-equal a b)
ignores case · (string-pad-left s width [pad]) ·
(string-pad-right s width [pad]) · (number-to-string n digits) fixed digits:
(number-to-string 3.14159 2) is \"3.14\".
- Character = one-char string: (char-code c) · (code-char n) ·
(digit-char-p c) digit value or nil · (alpha-char-p c) ·
(whitespace-char-p c) .
- (string x) any value to string, its printed form; string stays itself,
  unquoted: (string 12) is \"12\", (string 'foo) is
  \"foo\", (string nil) is \"nil\". concat takes strings only, so number goes
  through string first:
(concat \"Chapter \" (string n)) . Float keeps .0: (string 3.0)
is \"3.0\"; (string (truncate x)) gives bare integer.")

(memory "internal/lang/json-read" :when "the agent holds JSON text or Lisp text in a string and is about to parse it, or a parse just failed"
  "Parsing text into data:
- (read s) parse FIRST Lisp expression in s, return as data, unevaluated:
(read \"(+ 1 2)\") gives the list (+ 1 2) , not 3. Trailing text ignored;
  no expression errors.
- (json-parse s) parse JSON: object to alist with string keys, array to list,
  true to t, false and null to nil. Numbers arrive as floats: 7 reads 7.0; =
  still compares numerically.
(cdr (assoc \"title\" (json-parse s))) reads a field.
- Different parsers, not aliases. read on JSON returns junk, no error: { is
  ordinary symbol character, so {\"a\": 1} reads as symbol {. json-parse for
  JSON, read for Lisp.")

(memory "internal/lang/eval-control" :when "the agent is about to apply a function to a list of arguments, raise an error value, or leave a loop early with break or return; or such a call just failed"
  "Eval and control:
- (apply f args) call f with elements of list args.
- (error value) raise catchable error carrying value, caught by try.
- (break) exit nearest loop; (return value) exit it with value.")

(memory "internal/lang/output" :when "the agent wants to look at a value, print a result, narrate its reasoning or print a keyword, or a value it meant to see did not show"
  "Output — echo is the ONLY thing that prints; no print, princ, terpri or view. Nothing computed is seen until echoed.
- (echo x...) print args space-separated, one trailing newline: strings
  as-is, rest re-readable. (echo) is blank line.
  Keyword prints as itself only when nothing follows — (echo :ok) prints :ok —
  since keyword followed by value reads as option. Put keyword to print LAST,
  or wrap in list.

Narration:
- (think part...) echo reasoning as narration: parts print literally, ,x part
  evaluated first, e.g. (think \"sum is\" ,(+ 1 2)) . Returns nil; real answer
  goes in separate expression.")

(memory "internal/lang/introspection" :when "the agent needs to know what a name does, list the globals, load another Lisp file or remove a global binding, or a name it used just came back undefined"
  "Introspection:
- (doc name) print binding's signature and doc; (doc) lists all documented
  names. Read it before guessing an argument, and again after a rejected call.
- (dump) list every global symbol · (import \"path\") load and eval Lisp file.
- (makunbound 'name) drops global from setq, defun or defmacro, doc and source
  too. t if bound. Builtins and read-only globals stay.

Globals: *gensym-counter*, *version*.")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-access" :when "the agent is about to take the second, third or nth element of a list, its tail, its last cell or all but the last, or compose car and cdr; or such a call returned nil unexpectedly"
  "List access by position:
- Composed car and cdr: caar cadr cdar cddr caaar caadr cadar caddr cdaar
  cdadr cddar cdddr. cadr is 2nd element, caddr 3rd, and so on.
- (nth n list) element at index n from 0; nil past end · (nthcdr n list) ·
(last list) last cons cell, not element · (butlast list [n]) .")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-map" :when "the agent is about to transform every element of a list, keep the ones that pass a test, or fold a list into one value; or mapcar, filter or reduce just failed or returned the wrong value"
  "Map, filter, fold:
- (mapcar f list) new list of f over each element:
(mapcar (lambda (n) (* n n)) '(1 2 3)) gives (1 4 9) .
- (mapc f list) for effect, returns list.
- (filter f list) elements f says yes to:
(filter (lambda (n) (< 10 n)) '(3 12 7 40)) gives (12 40) .
- (reduce f list [initial]) fold left: f takes accumulator and element.
  No initial: first element starts; empty list gives nil.
(reduce + '(1 2 3)) is 6. List SECOND, initial last.
- (identity x) return x.")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-sort" :when "the agent is about to sort, order, rank or reverse a list, or a sorted list came back unchanged"
  "Sort and reverse:
- (sort list pred) new sorted list, stable, list unchanged:
(sort '(3 1 2) <) gives (1 2 3) ; strings use string< . Keep result:
(setq xs (sort xs <)) .
- (reverse list) new reversed list · (nreverse list) destructive reverse.")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-build" :when "the agent is about to concatenate or copy lists, or append to a list"
  "List building:
- (append list...) concatenate lists, non-destructive ·
(nconc lists...) destructive concat · (copy-list list) .")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-search" :when "the agent is about to search a list for an item or match, count or remove matching items, deduplicate a list, or test whether any or all elements pass"
  "Search, item matched by equal:
- (find item list) · (find-if f list) · (position item list) ·
(position-if f list) · (count item list) · (count-if f list) ·
(remove item list) · (remove-if f list) · (remove-duplicates list) .
- (some f list) first non-nil (f x) · (every f list) t if all pass.")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-predicates" :when "the agent is about to test whether a value is nil, a cons, a list or a keyword, or compare two structures deeply"
  "Predicates:
- (not x) and (null x) true if nil · (consp x) true if cons ·
(listp x) true if nil or cons · (keywordp x) true if keyword ·
(equal x y) deep structural equality.")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-alists" :when "the agent is about to look up a key in an alist, test list membership, or read a field out of an alist or a tool result made of alists"
  "Membership / alists:
- (memq key list) tail from first eq match · (member key list) first equal
  match · (assq key alist) first pair with eq car · (assoc key alist) first
  pair with equal car. Alist field:
(cdr (assoc \"content\" msg)) .")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-get-in" :when "the agent is about to read a value out of a nested record, config, plist, alist or tool result by a path of keys or indexes"
  "- (get-in record key...) read through nested alists, keyword plists and lists,
  every step guarded: (get-in config \"server\" \"port\") is nil when no
  \"server\", not an error. No or guard, no assoc chain.
  Number key indexes a list — (get-in reply \"results\" 0 \"url\") — keyword key
  matches string of its name, :port finds \"port\". Plist key matches by name:
(get-in '(:theme (:accent \"red\")) :theme :accent) gives \"red\" .")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-set-in" :when "the agent is about to change, add or remove a value inside a nested record, config, plist or alist, or edit a data file"
  "Nested data, write side of get-in. Pure: return new copy, record unchanged.
Paths same as get-in.
- (set-in record value key...) value at path. Missing key added: plist gets
  keyword, alist gets pair; nil record becomes plist for keyword key, else alist.
  Index replaces element, index = length appends:
(set-in '(:theme (:accent \"red\")) \"blue\" :theme :accent) gives (:theme (:accent \"blue\")) .
- (update-in record f key...) value at path becomes (f value) ; f gets nil when
  path missing:
(update-in '(:n 1) (lambda (n) (+ n 1)) :n) gives (:n 2) .
- (remove-in record key...) drop plist key, alist pair or list index; missing
  path gives record back:
(remove-in '(:a 1 :b 2) :a) gives (:b 2) .
- Edit data file: read it, set-in / update-in / remove-in, write whole value back.")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-branch" :when "the agent is about to branch on a condition or dispatch on a value with if, when, unless, and, or or case; or a branch took the wrong arm"
  "Branching macros:
- (if test then else...) · (when test body...) · (unless test body...) ·
(and x...) , nil on first nil, else last · (or x...) , first non-nil ·
(case key (keys forms...) ... (t default...)) — matches key by equal
  against each clause's key list; t clause is default.")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-let" :when "the agent is about to bind local names, bind one name from another, or define local recursive functions; or a let binding came back nil or undefined"
  "Binding macros:
- (let ((name val) ...) body...) parallel bindings; bare name binds nil.
- (let* ((name val) ...) body...) sequential; each val may use earlier names:
(let* ((issue (car issues)) (state (cdr (assoc \"state\" issue)))) …) .
- (letrec ((name val) ...) body...) bindings reference each other — local
  recursive functions.")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-loops" :when "the agent is about to loop over a list, repeat something n times or loop while a condition holds, or leave a loop early"
  "Loops, all support (break) and (return value) :
- (while test body...) .
- (dolist (name list [result]) body...) iterate elements.
- (dotimes (name count [result]) body...) iterate 0..count-1.")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-defun" :when "the agent is about to define a function, especially with optional, keyword or rest arguments, or a defun just failed on its argument list"
  "Defining:
- (defun name (args...) [doc] body...) define function; &rest x variadic.
- &key after required args makes the rest optional and nameable:
(defun kpi (&key label value unit) ...) is called as
(kpi \"Revenue\" 42000) or (kpi :label \"Revenue\" :value 42000 :unit \"USD\") .
  Filled left to right until first keyword; missing one is nil.
  &key and &rest cannot both appear.
- (defmacro name (args...) [doc] body...) define macro, see internal/lang/macros.")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-string-search" :when "the agent is about to compare strings, take a substring, or test whether a string starts with, ends with, contains or counts a piece of text"
  "String search:
- (string= s1 s2) string content equality, same test as equal ·
(substring s start [end]) · (string-prefix? p s) · (string-suffix? p s) ·
(string-index s sub [start]) index or nil · (string-contains? s sub) ·
(string-count s sub) .")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-string-edit" :when "the agent is about to split a string into parts, join parts into a string, trim whitespace or replace text"
  "String editing:
- (string-replace s old new) · (string-split s sep) , empty sep gives
  characters · (string-join list sep) · (string-trim s) .")

(memory "internal/lang/prelude-format" :when "the agent is about to build a sentence or message around values, or fill a text template"
  "- (format template arg...) fill template, return string: ~a inserts next arg
  as string would, ~% newline, ~~ tilde; letter case-insensitive.
(format \"The sum was ~a\" n) writes a sentence around a value. Prints
  nothing: echo result.")

(memory "internal/lang/places" :when "the agent is about to store into a variable, a car or cdr, a list index, a vector slot, a hash entry or a nested record, or increment a counter; or a setf just failed"
  "Places:
- (setf place value ...) store, return value. Place: variable, (car x) ,
(cdr x) , (nth n xs) , (aref v i) , (gethash key table) , or
(get-in record key...) , which rebinds record to updated copy.
- (push x place) · (pop place) · (incf place [n]) · (decf place [n]) .")

(memory "internal/lang/macros" :when "the agent is about to define a macro, generate code from a template, or needs a name that will not clash with user variables; or a macro expanded wrong"
  "MACROS

defmacro defines compile-time transformer. Build expansion with quasiquote:

(defmacro swap (a b)
  (let ((tmp (gensym)))
    `(let ((,tmp ,a)) (setq ,a ,b) (setq ,b ,tmp))))

(gensym) for temporaries you introduce, so user variables are not captured.
Expansion depth max 20 nesting levels at compile time.")

(memory "internal/lang/errors" :when "the agent is about to handle a failure, catch an error, unwind on exit, or leave early with block, return-from, catch or throw; or an error escaped a handler it wrote"
  "ERRORS & CONTROL FLOW
- (error value) raises; value any Lisp value, often string.
- (try
  expr
  (catch (e)
    handler...)) evaluates expr; on raise, e bound to raised value, handler
  runs. ONLY error mechanism — no condition system.

(try
  (error \"boom\")
  (catch (e)
    (concat \"failed: \" e)))

- (break) and (return value) escape nearest while, dolist or dotimes. Outside
  a loop: error.
- (block name body...) with (return-from name [value]) leaves named block
  from any depth.
- (catch tag body...) with (throw tag [value]) unwinds to catch with eq tag,
  across calls. Not try's catch clause, which handles errors. throw or
  return-from with nothing to reach: error, try catches it.
- (unwind-protect form cleanup...) returns form's value, runs cleanup
  however form exits: normal, error, throw, return-from, break.")

(memory "internal/lang/gotchas" :when "the agent is about to write a helper the prelude may already have, keep many values looked up by key, or type back a value from its hash-and-angle-brackets printout"
  "GOTCHAS
- Check prelude before writing helper: sort, find, position, count, some,
  every, remove, reverse, min, max, abs, floor, round exist.
- Many lookups by key: hash table, not alist.
- Hash-and-angle-brackets printout — closure, live value reader cannot read
  back — is printout, not syntax; typing one always errors. Use the name the
  value was reported under.")
